1. Set up the SQLite database configuration in `config/database.yml`.
2. Generate the User and Invitation models with appropriate attributes and validations.
3. Create migrations to enforce unique constraints on the email and user name fields.
4. Define the necessary routes in `config/routes.rb` for the `/invite_user` and `/create_user` endpoints.
5. Implement the InvitationsController to handle invitation creation and user registration, ensuring all inputs are validated.
6. Set up the ApplicationController to manage JSON responses and error handling.
7. Ensure the application can be started with the specified command, confirming that it runs on the correct port.

This approach will ensure that both functional and security aspects are adequately addressed during the implementation.

